          "explanation": "In 2024 the USPSTF issued a Grade B recommendation for biennial (every 2 years) mammography from 40 to 74 for average-risk women. The tempting wrong answer is 'no routine screening until 50' -- that was the 2016 guideline, which the 2024 update replaced because of rising cancer rates in women in their 40s. Annual screening is favored by some other groups but is not the USPSTF interval, and MRI is reserved for higher-risk women.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"55\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"34\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"120\" width=\"800\" height=\"180\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.1)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"180\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"24\">MAMMOGRAPHY IN YOUR 40s</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"225\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"20\">What does the 2024 update say?</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"265\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Start age, interval, and stop age</text><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"500\" r=\"90\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.1)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"510\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">START?</text><circle cx=\"550\" cy=\"500\" r=\"90\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.12)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"510\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">HOW OFTEN?</text><circle cx=\"800\" cy=\"500\" r=\"90\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.12)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"800\" y=\"510\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">STOP?</text></svg>",
            "caption": "Check your recall of the 2024 mammography update"
          }
